From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyDevices <pydevices@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] usb_host: full- and low-speed devices behind a high-speed
 hub, through its transaction translator

A full- or low-speed device behind a high-speed hub was refused. It is now
reached through the hub's transaction translator with split transactions.

The hub driver works out each device's translator (the high-speed hub's
address and port, inherited through full-speed hubs) and the USB host
library carries it into every pipe of the device. The HCD programs HCSPLT
for those pipes.

The DWC_OTG cannot issue split transactions in Scatter/Gather DMA mode:
a split control transfer completes its setup stage and then never
completes its data stage. With USB_HOST_DWC_SPLIT_TRANSACTIONS (on by
default on the ESP32-P4 and ESP32-S31) a high-speed host port therefore
runs in Buffer DMA mode. The HCD still fills and parses the same QTD lists;
a small engine executes them, one channel run per QTD (per packet for a
split), writes each QTD's status back as the DMA would, and reports the
same channel events. It handles the split handshakes (start split ACK,
complete split NYET, NAK restarts) and starts periodic channels from the
SOF interrupt following the frame list, since Buffer DMA mode has no
periodic scheduler.

A halt never abandons a split whose start split the translator took: the
translator has already answered the device, so its data exists only there.
The complete split runs first, also for a bulk or control complete split
still waiting for its microframe when the halt is asked for, and a bulk
transfer that has moved bytes when the halt lands completes short with them
instead of being canceled. A bulk or control complete split that sees a
transaction error is asked again, as the translator keeps the result until
it is collected.

A bulk or control split the device NAKs is asked again in the next frame,
so an idle endpoint costs one retry a millisecond. For the first few NAKs
after data moved it is asked again a microframe later instead: a device
that NAKs between packets, as one whose firmware arms its endpoint a packet
at a time does, would otherwise be held to one packet a millisecond.

A bulk or control split that fails with transaction errors can leave its
transaction in the translator's buffer. The HCD then owes the translator a
Clear_TT_Buffer request (USB 2.0, 11.24.2.3): it queues the request on the
port and tells the hub driver through the port callback, and the hub driver
sends it on the translator's hub's control pipe from its own task, one at a
time, as Linux does.

A bulk or control complete split answered NYET is asked again in the next
microframe, from the SOF interrupt, rather than at once: asking at once was
only answered NYET again, and cost an interrupt each time.

Isochronous splits run one packet per frame. An OUT packet goes to the
translator as start splits of up to 188 bytes in consecutive microframes
(BEGIN, MID..., END, or ALL when it fits in one). An IN packet is asked for
with one start split, and complete splits from two microframes later collect
it: NYET while nothing has arrived yet, MDATA with each part while more is to
come. Each part lands in a buffer of the pipe's own and is copied on, since
the translator's part sizes can leave the next one at an address the DMA
can't write to.
Each part is timed from the microframe the last run was started for, not
from when its interrupt is handled: behind high-speed traffic, such as a
drive reading on the same port, that interrupt can come a microframe late,
and complete splits a microframe behind miss the end of the packet.

The translator's full-speed frame is budgeted. Each periodic endpoint behind
a translator is charged its worst-case bus time (USB 2.0, 5.11.3) against
90% of the frame, and each isochronous endpoint is given microframes of its
own for what the translator runs for it, 188 bytes to a microframe, so an IN
and an OUT stream don't collide in the translator. A pipe that doesn't fit is
refused with ESP_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED and an error log saying why.

Not done: the budget charges every periodic endpoint in every frame,
whatever its interval, and a translator serves one isochronous OUT endpoint.
---
diff --git a/Kconfig b/Kconfig
index 29c9a68..9680951 100644
--- a/Kconfig
+++ b/Kconfig
@@ -235,6 +235,19 @@ menu "USB-OTG"
             accessing external RAM.
         # Todo: IDF-11368 (aligned memory alloc size)
 
+    config USB_HOST_DWC_SPLIT_TRANSACTIONS
+        depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4 || IDF_TARGET_ESP32S31
+        bool "Full- and low-speed devices behind a high-speed hub (split transactions)"
+        default y
+        help
+            A full- or low-speed device behind a high-speed hub is reached through the hub's transaction
+            translator, using split transactions. The USB-DWC can only issue split transactions in Buffer DMA
+            mode, so with this option the high-speed host port runs in Buffer DMA mode instead of Scatter/Gather
+            DMA mode. The driver then starts each transaction from its interrupt handler, and periodic transfers
+            from the start of frame interrupt, which costs more CPU time than Scatter/Gather DMA.
+
+            When disabled, a full- or low-speed device behind a high-speed hub is refused.
+
     # Hidden or compatibility options
     config USB_OTG_SUPPORTED
         # Invisible config kept for compatibility
diff --git a/private_include/ext_hub.h b/private_include/ext_hub.h
index aee4f6e..ed1ff85 100644
--- a/private_include/ext_hub.h
+++ b/private_include/ext_hub.h
@@ -106,6 +106,44 @@ esp_err_t ext_hub_get_speed(ext_hub_handle_t ext_hub_hdl, usb_speed_t *speed);
  */
 hcd_port_handle_t ext_hub_get_root_port(ext_hub_handle_t ext_hub_hdl);
 
+/**
+ * @brief Send a Clear_TT_Buffer request to a high-speed hub's transaction translator
+ *
+ * Clears the translator's buffer that a failed bulk or control split transaction may have left busy (USB 2.0,
+ * 11.24.2.3). The request is sent on the hub's control pipe on its own transfer, after any sent before it; a control
+ * endpoint's buffer is cleared for both directions.
+ *
+ * @note Called from the USB Host Library's task, like the rest of the External Hub Driver's processing
+ *
+ * @param[in] hub_addr Address of the hub
+ * @param[in] value wValue: the endpoint's number (bits 3..0), device address (10..4), type (12..11) and direction (15)
+ *
+ * @return
+ *    - ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND if no configured hub has that address
+ *    - ESP_ERR_NO_MEM if the transfer could not be allocated
+ *    - ESP_OK if the request was queued
+ */
+esp_err_t ext_hub_clear_tt_buffer(uint8_t hub_addr, uint16_t value);
+
+/**
+ * @brief Get the transaction translator that serves a device on one of an External Hub's ports
+ *
+ * A full- or low-speed device on a high-speed hub is reached through that hub's transaction translator. A device on
+ * a full-speed hub that is itself behind a high-speed hub shares the translator that serves the full-speed hub.
+ *
+ * @param[in] ext_hub_hdl External Hub device handle
+ * @param[in] port_num Port number (1-based)
+ * @param[in] port_speed Speed of the device on that port
+ * @param[out] tt_hub_addr Address of the high-speed hub whose transaction translator serves the device, 0 if none
+ * @param[out] tt_port_num That hub's port, 0 if none
+ *
+ * @return
+ *    - ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG if a pointer is NULL
+ *    - ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND if the hub is not found
+ *    - ESP_OK if the translator was obtained
+ */
+esp_err_t ext_hub_get_port_tt(ext_hub_handle_t ext_hub_hdl, uint8_t port_num, usb_speed_t port_speed, uint8_t *tt_hub_addr, uint8_t *tt_port_num);
+
 /**
  * @brief Add new device
  *
diff --git a/private_include/hcd.h b/private_include/hcd.h
index 42cf016..022bade 100644
--- a/private_include/hcd.h
+++ b/private_include/hcd.h
@@ -195,8 +195,19 @@ typedef struct {
     const usb_ep_desc_t *ep_desc;           /**< Pointer to endpoint descriptor of the pipe */
     usb_speed_t dev_speed;                  /**< Speed of the device */
     uint8_t dev_addr;                       /**< Device address of the pipe */
+    uint8_t tt_hub_addr;                    /**< Address of the high-speed hub whose transaction translator serves a full- or low-speed device, 0 if none */
+    uint8_t tt_port_num;                    /**< That hub's port the device is behind (1-based), 0 if none */
 } hcd_pipe_config_t;
 
+/**
+ * @brief A Clear_TT_Buffer request a transaction translator is owed (USB 2.0, 11.24.2.3)
+ */
+typedef struct {
+    uint8_t hub_addr;       /**< Address of the high-speed hub whose translator it is */
+    uint8_t tt_port;        /**< The hub's port the failed transfer's device is behind */
+    uint16_t value;         /**< wValue: the endpoint's number, device address, type and direction */
+} hcd_tt_clear_t;
+
 // ---------------------------------------------------- HCD Port -------------------------------------------------------
 
 /**
@@ -281,6 +292,19 @@ hcd_port_state_t hcd_port_get_state(hcd_port_handle_t port_hdl);
  */
 esp_err_t hcd_port_get_speed(hcd_port_handle_t port_hdl, usb_speed_t *speed);
 
+/**
+ * @brief Take the next Clear_TT_Buffer request the port owes a transaction translator
+ *
+ * A bulk or control transfer to a device behind a translator that fails with transaction errors can leave its
+ * transaction in the translator's buffer. The port then calls its callback (with HCD_PORT_EVENT_NONE, if it has no
+ * other event), and the hub driver takes each request with this and sends it to the translator's hub.
+ *
+ * @param[in] port_hdl Port handle
+ * @param[out] tt_clear The request
+ * @return true if a request was taken
+ */
+bool hcd_port_get_tt_clear(hcd_port_handle_t port_hdl, hcd_tt_clear_t *tt_clear);
+
 /**
  * @brief Handle a ports event
  *
diff --git a/private_include/usbh.h b/private_include/usbh.h
index 5d66f3f..e00b63e 100644
--- a/private_include/usbh.h
+++ b/private_include/usbh.h
@@ -162,6 +162,8 @@ typedef struct {
     hcd_port_handle_t root_port_hdl;        /**< Handle of the port that the device is connected to */
     usb_device_handle_t parent_dev_hdl;     /**< Parent's device handle */
     uint8_t parent_port_num;                /**< Parent's port number */
+    uint8_t tt_hub_addr;                    /**< Address of the high-speed hub whose transaction translator serves this full- or low-speed device, 0 if none */
+    uint8_t tt_port_num;                    /**< That hub's port the device is behind (1-based), 0 if none */
 } usbh_dev_params_t;
 
 // ---------------------- USBH Processing Functions ----------------------------
@@ -443,6 +445,19 @@ esp_err_t usbh_dev_get_info(usb_device_handle_t dev_hdl, usb_device_info_t *dev_
  */
 esp_err_t usbh_dev_get_root_port_hdl(usb_device_handle_t dev_hdl, hcd_port_handle_t *root_port_hdl);
 
+/**
+ * @brief Get the transaction translator a full- or low-speed device is reached through
+ *
+ * @param[in] dev_hdl Device handle
+ * @param[out] tt_hub_addr Address of the high-speed hub whose transaction translator serves the device, 0 if none
+ * @param[out] tt_port_num That hub's port the device is behind, 0 if none
+ *
+ * @return
+ *    - ESP_OK: Transaction translator obtained successfully
+ *    - ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG: Invalid argument
+ */
+esp_err_t usbh_dev_get_tt(usb_device_handle_t dev_hdl, uint8_t *tt_hub_addr, uint8_t *tt_port_num);
+
 /**
  * @brief Get a device's device descriptor
  *
diff --git a/src/ext_hub.c b/src/ext_hub.c
index ed4b4ba..51da12c 100644
--- a/src/ext_hub.c
+++ b/src/ext_hub.c
@@ -84,8 +84,11 @@ typedef enum {
     DEV_ACTION_ERROR                    = (1 << 6),  /**< Device encounters an error */
     DEV_ACTION_RELEASE                  = (1 << 7),  /**< Device should be released */
     DEV_ACTION_FREE                     = (1 << 8),  /**< Device should be freed */
+    DEV_ACTION_TT_CLEAR                 = (1 << 9),  /**< Device's Clear_TT_Buffer request completed */
 } dev_action_t;
 
+#define EXT_HUB_TT_CLEARS_MAX           8   /**< Clear_TT_Buffer requests a hub holds while one is on its way */
+
 typedef struct ext_hub_s ext_hub_dev_t;
 
 /**
@@ -119,6 +122,9 @@ struct ext_hub_s {
         ext_hub_stage_t stage;                      /**< Device's stage */
         uint8_t maxchild;                           /**< Amount of allocated ports. Could be 0 for some Hubs. Is increased when new port is added and decreased when port has been freed. */
         ext_hub_state_t state;                      /**< Device's state */
+        uint16_t tt_values[EXT_HUB_TT_CLEARS_MAX];  /**< Clear_TT_Buffer requests waiting to be sent (wValue each) */
+        uint8_t tt_num;                             /**< How many wait */
+        bool tt_busy;                               /**< A Clear_TT_Buffer request is on its way */
     } single_thread;                                /**< Single thread members don't require a critical section, as long as they are never accessed from multiple threads */
 
     struct {
@@ -129,6 +135,8 @@ struct ext_hub_s {
         usb_device_handle_t dev_hdl;                /**< Device's handle */
         urb_t *ctrl_urb;                            /**< Device's Control pipe transfer URB */
         urb_t *in_urb;                              /**< Device's Interrupt pipe URB */
+        urb_t *tt_urb;                              /**< Clear_TT_Buffer requests' URB, allocated at the first. Kept apart from
+                                                         ctrl_urb, which the hub's own requests use, so it can go between them */
         usbh_ep_handle_t ep_in_hdl;                 /**< Device's Interrupt EP handle */
 
         usb_hub_descriptor_t *hub_desc;             /**< Device's Hub descriptor pointer. Could be NULL when not requested */
@@ -256,6 +264,19 @@ static void control_transfer_complete_cb(usb_transfer_t *ctrl_xfer)
     }
 }
 
+static void tt_clear_complete_cb(usb_transfer_t *tt_xfer)
+{
+    ext_hub_dev_t *ext_hub_dev = (ext_hub_dev_t *) tt_xfer->context;
+
+    EXT_HUB_ENTER_CRITICAL();
+    bool call_proc_req_cb = _device_set_actions(ext_hub_dev, DEV_ACTION_TT_CLEAR);
+    EXT_HUB_EXIT_CRITICAL();
+
+    if (call_proc_req_cb) {
+        p_ext_hub_driver->constant.proc_req_cb(false, p_ext_hub_driver->constant.proc_req_cb_arg);
+    }
+}
+
 static void interrupt_transfer_complete_cb(usb_transfer_t *intr_xfer)
 {
     assert(intr_xfer);
@@ -784,9 +805,58 @@ static void device_free(ext_hub_dev_t *ext_hub_dev)
 
     urb_free(ext_hub_dev->constant.ctrl_urb);
     urb_free(ext_hub_dev->constant.in_urb);
+    if (ext_hub_dev->constant.tt_urb != NULL && !ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_busy) {
+        urb_free(ext_hub_dev->constant.tt_urb);
+    }
     heap_caps_free(ext_hub_dev);
 }
 
+/**
+ * @brief Send the next waiting Clear_TT_Buffer request, if none is on its way
+ */
+static void tt_clear_send_next(ext_hub_dev_t *ext_hub_dev)
+{
+    if (ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_busy || ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_num == 0
+            || ext_hub_dev->dynamic.flags.is_gone || ext_hub_dev->dynamic.flags.waiting_release
+            || ext_hub_dev->dynamic.flags.waiting_free) {
+        return;
+    }
+    uint16_t value = ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_values[0];
+    ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_num--;
+    memmove(&ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_values[0], &ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_values[1],
+            ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_num * sizeof(uint16_t));
+    usb_transfer_t *transfer = &ext_hub_dev->constant.tt_urb->transfer;
+    usb_setup_packet_t *setup = (usb_setup_packet_t *)transfer->data_buffer;
+    setup->bmRequestType = USB_BM_REQUEST_TYPE_DIR_OUT | USB_BM_REQUEST_TYPE_TYPE_CLASS | USB_BM_REQUEST_TYPE_RECIP_OTHER;
+    setup->bRequest = USB_B_REQUEST_HUB_CLEAR_TT_BUFFER;
+    setup->wValue = value;
+    setup->wIndex = 1;  // A single translator (the hub's default interface setting), named 1
+    setup->wLength = 0;
+    transfer->num_bytes = sizeof(usb_setup_packet_t);
+    ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_busy = true;
+    esp_err_t ret = usbh_dev_submit_ctrl_urb(ext_hub_dev->constant.dev_hdl, ext_hub_dev->constant.tt_urb);
+    if (ret != ESP_OK) {
+        ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_busy = false;
+        ESP_LOGE(EXT_HUB_TAG, "[%d] Clear_TT_Buffer 0x%04x: failed to submit: %s", ext_hub_dev->constant.dev_addr, value,
+                 esp_err_to_name(ret));
+    }
+}
+
+static void handle_tt_clear(ext_hub_dev_t *ext_hub_dev)
+{
+    usb_transfer_t *transfer = &ext_hub_dev->constant.tt_urb->transfer;
+    const usb_setup_packet_t *setup = (const usb_setup_packet_t *)transfer->data_buffer;
+    ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_busy = false;
+    if (transfer->status == USB_TRANSFER_STATUS_COMPLETED) {
+        ESP_LOGI(EXT_HUB_TAG, "[%d] Cleared the translator's buffer for device %d EP %d", ext_hub_dev->constant.dev_addr,
+                 (setup->wValue >> 4) & 0x7F, setup->wValue & 0x0F);
+    } else {
+        ESP_LOGW(EXT_HUB_TAG, "[%d] Clear_TT_Buffer 0x%04x: status %d", ext_hub_dev->constant.dev_addr, setup->wValue,
+                 transfer->status);
+    }
+    tt_clear_send_next(ext_hub_dev);
+}
+
 static bool dev_is_in_list(ext_hub_dev_t *ext_hub_dev)
 {
     bool is_in_list = false;
@@ -1324,6 +1394,72 @@ esp_err_t ext_hub_get_speed(ext_hub_handle_t ext_hub_hdl, usb_speed_t *speed)
     return ESP_OK;
 }
 
+esp_err_t ext_hub_clear_tt_buffer(uint8_t hub_addr, uint16_t value)
+{
+    EXT_HUB_ENTER_CRITICAL();
+    EXT_HUB_CHECK_FROM_CRIT(p_ext_hub_driver != NULL, ESP_ERR_NOT_ALLOWED);
+    ext_hub_dev_t *ext_hub_dev = NULL;
+    ext_hub_dev_t *hub;
+    TAILQ_FOREACH(hub, &p_ext_hub_driver->dynamic.ext_hubs_tailq, dynamic.tailq_entry) {
+        if (hub->constant.dev_addr == hub_addr) {
+            ext_hub_dev = hub;
+        }
+    }
+    TAILQ_FOREACH(hub, &p_ext_hub_driver->dynamic.ext_hubs_pending_tailq, dynamic.tailq_entry) {
+        if (hub->constant.dev_addr == hub_addr) {
+            ext_hub_dev = hub;
+        }
+    }
+    EXT_HUB_EXIT_CRITICAL();
+    EXT_HUB_CHECK(ext_hub_dev != NULL, ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND);
+    EXT_HUB_CHECK(ext_hub_dev->single_thread.state == EXT_HUB_STATE_CONFIGURED, ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE);
+
+    if (ext_hub_dev->constant.tt_urb == NULL) {
+        ext_hub_dev->constant.tt_urb = urb_alloc(sizeof(usb_setup_packet_t), 0);
+        EXT_HUB_CHECK(ext_hub_dev->constant.tt_urb != NULL, ESP_ERR_NO_MEM);
+        // Client is a memory address of the p_ext_hub_driver driver object, as for the hub's other transfers
+        ext_hub_dev->constant.tt_urb->usb_host_client = (void *) p_ext_hub_driver;
+        ext_hub_dev->constant.tt_urb->transfer.callback = tt_clear_complete_cb;
+        ext_hub_dev->constant.tt_urb->transfer.context = (void *)ext_hub_dev;
+        ext_hub_dev->constant.tt_urb->transfer.timeout_ms = 1000;
+    }
+    // A control endpoint's translator buffer is cleared for both directions (as Linux does)
+    const bool ctrl = ((value >> 11) & 3) == 0;
+    for (int dir = 0; dir < (ctrl ? 2 : 1); dir++) {
+        uint16_t v = dir ? (value ^ 0x8000) : value;
+        bool waiting = false;
+        for (int i = 0; i < ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_num; i++) {
+            waiting |= ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_values[i] == v;
+        }
+        if (!waiting && ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_num < EXT_HUB_TT_CLEARS_MAX) {
+            ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_values[ext_hub_dev->single_thread.tt_num++] = v;
+        }
+    }
+    tt_clear_send_next(ext_hub_dev);
+    return ESP_OK;
+}
+
+esp_err_t ext_hub_get_port_tt(ext_hub_handle_t ext_hub_hdl, uint8_t port_num, usb_speed_t port_speed, uint8_t *tt_hub_addr, uint8_t *tt_port_num)
+{
+    EXT_HUB_CHECK(ext_hub_hdl != NULL && tt_hub_addr != NULL && tt_port_num != NULL, ESP_ERR_INVALID_ARG);
+    EXT_HUB_CHECK(dev_is_in_list(ext_hub_hdl), ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND);
+    ext_hub_dev_t *ext_hub_dev = (ext_hub_dev_t *)ext_hub_hdl;
+    usb_device_info_t dev_info;
+    ESP_ERROR_CHECK(usbh_dev_get_info(ext_hub_dev->constant.dev_hdl, &dev_info));
+    *tt_hub_addr = 0;
+    *tt_port_num = 0;
+    if (dev_info.speed == USB_SPEED_HIGH) {
+        // A high-speed hub translates for the full- and low-speed devices on its own ports
+        if (port_speed != USB_SPEED_HIGH) {
+            *tt_hub_addr = ext_hub_dev->constant.dev_addr;
+            *tt_port_num = port_num;
+        }
+        return ESP_OK;
+    }
+    // A full-speed hub behind a high-speed one: its devices share the translator that serves the hub
+    return usbh_dev_get_tt(ext_hub_dev->constant.dev_hdl, tt_hub_addr, tt_port_num);
+}
+
 hcd_port_handle_t ext_hub_get_root_port(ext_hub_handle_t ext_hub_hdl)
 {
     EXT_HUB_CHECK(ext_hub_hdl != NULL, NULL);
@@ -1532,6 +1668,9 @@ esp_err_t ext_hub_process(void)
         if (action_flags & DEV_ACTION_EP1_CLEAR) {
             handle_ep1_clear(ext_hub_dev);
         }
+        if (action_flags & DEV_ACTION_TT_CLEAR) {
+            handle_tt_clear(ext_hub_dev);
+        }
         if (action_flags & DEV_ACTION_ERROR) {
             handle_error(ext_hub_dev);
         }
diff --git a/src/hcd_dwc.c b/src/hcd_dwc.c
index 8dad6d8..0beee6d 100644
--- a/src/hcd_dwc.c
+++ b/src/hcd_dwc.c
@@ -143,6 +143,13 @@ DEFINE_CRIT_SECTION_LOCK_STATIC(hcd_lock);
 #define CACHE_SYNC_DATA_BUFFER_C2M(pipe, urb)
 #endif // CACHED_MEMORY_SYNC
 
+#if CONFIG_USB_HOST_DWC_SPLIT_TRANSACTIONS
+#define HCD_BUFFER_DMA                              1
+#define HCD_TT_CLEARS_MAX                           4   // Clear_TT_Buffer requests a port holds for its hub driver
+#else
+#define HCD_BUFFER_DMA                              0
+#endif
+
 // ------------------------------------------------------ Types --------------------------------------------------------
 
 typedef struct pipe_obj pipe_t;
@@ -192,6 +199,40 @@ typedef struct {
     } status_flags;                         // Status flags for the buffer
 } dma_buffer_block_t;
 
+#if HCD_BUFFER_DMA
+typedef enum {
+    BD_STATE_IDLE,      // Not executing a buffer
+    BD_STATE_RUN,       // The channel is enabled
+    BD_STATE_WAIT,      // Waiting for a (micro)frame to start the channel in
+} bd_state_t;
+
+/**
+ * @brief Buffer DMA mode: where a pipe's channel is in executing its QTD list
+ */
+typedef struct {
+    void *list;                     // QTD list being executed
+    dma_buffer_block_t *buffer;     // Buffer the list belongs to
+    int len;                        // Length of the list
+    int idx;                        // Current QTD
+    int stop_idx;                   // QTD index reported when the buffer is done
+    int hoc_idx;                    // Isochronous: the last QTD of the buffer
+    int interval;                   // Isochronous: QTD spacing
+    uint32_t done;                  // Bytes of the current QTD moved so far
+    uint32_t run_len;               // Bytes the channel was started with
+    uint32_t run_pkts;              // Packets the channel was started with
+    uint8_t errors;                 // Consecutive transaction errors
+    uint8_t nyets;                  // Complete splits answered NYET
+    uint8_t quick_naks;             // Split NAKs still retried in the next microframe rather than the next frame
+    uint16_t at;                    // Isochronous split: the microframe the next run waits for (with at_set)
+    uint16_t uf;                    // Isochronous split: the microframe the current run was started for
+    bd_state_t state;
+    uint8_t csplit: 1;              // The next run is a complete split
+    uint8_t ping: 1;                // The next OUT run starts with PING
+    uint8_t halt_req: 1;            // A halt was requested
+    uint8_t at_set: 1;              // Isochronous split: the next run waits for microframe "at"
+} bdma_t;
+#endif // HCD_BUFFER_DMA
+
 /**
  * @brief Object representing a pipe in the HCD layer
  */
@@ -220,6 +261,18 @@ struct pipe_obj {
     // HAL related
     usb_dwc_hal_chan_t *chan_obj;
